
# Event Service (Spring Boot)

Manages event creation, updates, listing, and internal seat management by admin

## Tech Stack
- Java 17
- Spring Boot
- Spring Web
- Spring Data JPA
- Spring Security (ADMIN for create/update/delete)
- postgreSQL

## Run Instructions

cd event-service
mvn clean install
mvn spring-boot:run


Runs at:
 http://localhost:8081

application.properties

spring.application.name=project 

spring.datasource.url=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/eventdb
spring.datasource.username=postgres
spring.datasource.password=password

spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update
spring.jpa.show-sql=true
spring.jpa.database-platform=org.hibernate.dialect.PostgreSQLDialect

Event Table

event_id      PK
name          VARCHAR
description   VARCHAR
event_date    DATETIME
price         DOUBLE
total_seats   INT



API Endpoints
POST /events/create (ADMIN)

{
  "name": "Rock Concert",
  "description": "Live music",
  "eventDate": "2025-02-15T18:00:00",
  "price": 200,
  "totalSeats": 100
}




PUT /events/update/{id} (ADMIN)
DELETE /events/delete/{id} (ADMIN)
GET /events/all
Returns all events.
GET /events/id/{id}
Returns a single event.

Internal APIs (Called from Booking Service)
POST /events/internal/updateSeats
POST /events/internal/restoreSeats
These are not protected by admin rules.




